(collections-b, batch A (evening) - list properties. docs/ledger/collections-b.md
 LST2-14, LST2-15, LST2-16, LST2-17, LST2-18, LST2-19, LST2-23
 (LANGUAGE.md:2975-2993, LANGUAGE.md:3004-3005). No leaf anywhere read a property off
 a LIST before this one - `'s length`/`'s empty` were only ever emitted
 on a map or a buffer. The naming helpers are 'gen buffer name' and kin
 (gen_buffers.vox): a generic word-pool allocator, not buffer-specific,
 and the brief for tonight's batch says to reuse it rather than spend a
 second pool on the same shape of witness.

 The element count (1..7) and every value are drawn fresh each call,
 never fixed, so a one-element list - where `'s first` and `'s last` are
 the same reading - turns up in the corpus alongside longer ones without
 being special-cased. LST2-23's agreement half is checked against
 `element 1 of`/`element N of` rather than against a second literal, so
 it is really comparing two INDEPENDENT reads of the list, not the
 generator's own arithmetic against itself.)

