(LST2-20 (gap in the manual, LANGUAGE.md:2987-2993, hand-verified against
 both compilers - see probes/collections-b/LST2-20.vox): on an EMPTY
 list, `first` and `last` each read 0 AND set the error flag, the same
 contract the manual states only for an out-of-range `element N of`;
 `length`/`size` stay 0 and `empty` stays true, none of the three raising
 the flag. A stale-error drain (a flag declared false, then `On error Set
 it to true` with nothing erroring in between) sits before the first
 read under test, so a flag some earlier, unrelated leaf left standing
 in the same program cannot be mistaken for this leaf's own finding -
 the same defensive shape gen_buffers.vox's growth/bounds leaves use.

 Top level only (see the reservation note above 'gen dispatch leaf'):
 two `On error` handlers, unsafe as a block's mandatory closer
 (PROCEDURE.md 6a).)

