(LST-47 (LANGUAGE.md:2562-2563, folds LST-48): `keys` and `values` each
 yield a FRESH list, in insertion order - checked four ways: the order
 itself (element N of the keys/values list matches the Nth entry
 written); that mutating the returned keys list does not touch the
 map's own length, and a second, independent read still shows the
 original first key untouched (freshness); that a fresh read after a
 REPLACE still shows the same order; and that a fresh read after an
 INSERT shows the new key landing LAST. The entry count (2 or 3) is
 drawn; 'the third key' defaults to 'the second key' when it is not
 used, which lets 'gen noun other than any of three' double as a
 two-word exclusion for free.)

