 both nested values are read back out with `'s "key"` and checked
 ENTRY-WISE - the list's two elements by position, the inner map's one
 entry through a captured holder (a quoted map-key access can't be
 interpolated directly into an ASSERT message without doubling its own
 quotes, the same reason 'gen leaf map insert and replace' captures
 first).

