(LST-67 (LANGUAGE.md:2658-2676): the guard idiom. `is a number` on a
 `For each` loop variable does not narrow its static type, so arithmetic
 on it is refused inside the guard exactly as outside - getting the
 element into a DECLARED variable via `element N of` is what makes
 `got add 1` legal. The number's position among the three elements is
 drawn, not fixed, so the leaf never always guards the same slot.

 Rework, 2026-08-30 (owner directive): the guarded number was a tame
 `'rng below' of 1000`; the arithmetic this row exists to prove legal
 means the magnitude cannot stay tame without missing the i64 boundary
 the row's own claim is meant to stress. 'gen extreme number' can draw
 exactly i64::MAX, in which case `add 1` wraps to i64::MIN - hand-
 verified (both compilers) that a Vox `add` wraps identically whether
 computed here, at generator time, or in the emitted program, so the
 computed 'the expected' and the runtime `got` always agree, wrapped
 value included; nothing here needed a clamp. The filler decimal moved
 from a hand-rolled `whole.frac` to 'gen extreme float' for the same
 reason, secondary since no assertion reads it.)

