    a number called 'the stride' is 'rng below' of 6 add 1.
    a number called 'tags shown' is 0.
    a text called 'the last possessive' is "".
    While 'tags shown' is less than 'how many tags',
        a number called 'the step' is 'tags shown' multiply 'the stride',
        a number called 'the slot' is 'the step' add 'the rotation',
        a number called 'the tag' is 'the slot' modulo 7,
        a text called 'the payload' is 'gen value payload' of 'the tag',
        a text called 'the literal' is 'gen value expression' of 'the tag' and 'the payload',
        a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen fresh noun',
        a text called 'the name' is 'gen written name' of 'the phrase',
        a text called 'the possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the phrase',
        a text called 'the type text' is 'gen dynamic type text' of 'the tag',
        a text called 'the tag it reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the possessive',
        'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the name'} is {'the literal'}.\n",
        a text called 'the type assertion' is "{indent}If {'the possessive'} type is not \"{'the type text'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-14: expected {'the type text'} got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the type assertion',
        Set 'the last possessive' to 'the possessive',
        Set 'tags shown' to 'tags shown' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the last possessive'} type.\n".

(VAL-21 (LANGUAGE.md:2851-2865): `nothing` is the absent value, and it
 can sit in a list slot, a map value, or a `value` local. All three
 positions in one leaf, each read back into a `value` local and asserted
 with `is nothing` - which LANGUAGE.md:2871 says is the test, there
 being no `is a nothing` predicate.

 A slot that is NOT the absent one is asserted too, in the opposite
 direction: a runtime that answered `is nothing` for everything would
 pass the first three assertions and fail this one.

 All three spellings are drawn ('gen value payload' of tag 6 does the
 drawing), because LANGUAGE.md:2869 says `nothing`, `null` and `nil`
 produce the identical value and picking one always would be a rule
 nobody wrote. Which slot of the list and which key of the map hold the
 absent value are drawn for the same reason.)

